---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Release Ritual Redesign | Ethan Nguyen">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-10">
    <header class="space-y-2">
      <a class="text-sm underline decoration-slate-300 hover:decoration-slate-600" href="/">← Back</a>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Release Ritual Redesign</h1>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        Standardized rituals to improve clarity, execution, and stakeholder confidence.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">The Problem</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
        Releases were inconsistent, updates were scattered, and stakeholders lacked a single source of truth.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Context</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-700">
        <li>Multiple teams shipping on different cadences</li>
        <li>Conflicting definitions of “ready” and “done”</li>
        <li>High coordination overhead near launch</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Solution</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-700">
        <li>Defined release stages + checklist</li>
        <li>Weekly release review ritual + owners</li>
        <li>Central release notes + comms template</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Results</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-700">
        <li>Fewer last-minute surprises (add your metric later)</li>
        <li>Clearer stakeholder comms + expectations</li>
        <li>More predictable shipping cadence</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What I Learned</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
        Rituals reduce uncertainty—when the process is trusted, teams move faster with less stress.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
